        ecrm:P3_has_note    "The long tie, or four-in-hand tie, evolved from the sailor’s tie. It was absorbed into civilian fashion for informal dress by the 1850s. As early as the 1870s such ties were made with a pre-formed knot, as seen in this example."@en ;
